%% Title: Engineering Actor Substitution: Baseline = Human Author; After = Blitzy
%% Legend:
%%   Shows the same compute function called twice with different (period, actor) parameters.
%%   This is the mechanical guarantee of identical methodology required by the user prompt:
%%     "MUST use identical methodology for before and after periods —
%%      same window alignment, same extraction logic, different date range."
%%   The only differences between baseline and after extraction are:
%%     1. period (the date range)
%%     2. actor (the engineering actor parameter — human author of each PR in baseline;
%%        Blitzy in after)
%%   All other inputs (window alignment, bot exclusion list, classifier order,
%%   span-bounding logic) are module-scope CONSTANTS and cannot diverge between periods.
%%   See AAP §0.5.6 and decision-log.md DL-012 for the rationale.
sequenceDiagram
    participant Pipeline as 09_compute_metrics.py
    participant Compute as compute_phase(period, actor)
    participant Data as data/metrics.json
    Note over Pipeline,Data: Identical extraction logic, parameterized by (date range, actor)
    Pipeline->>Compute: compute_phase(period=baseline, actor=human_author_of_each_PR)
    Compute-->>Data: baseline metric values (per-actor breakdown by human author)
    Pipeline->>Compute: compute_phase(period=after, actor=Blitzy)
    Compute-->>Data: after metric values (Blitzy as single row + humans alongside)
    Note over Compute,Data: Same compute function, same module-scope constants
    Note over Compute,Data: (windows, exclusions, classifier, span-bounding logic)
